      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Monitor competitor prices from a URL list using AI extraction and Slack alerts\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs a daily check of competitor product pages listed in Google Sheets. It loops through each URL, fetches the page, uses AI to extract price and stock details, then compares the result against stored history. It sends Slack alerts for fetch failures, low-confidence AI results, and significant price drops, logs drops in Notion, updates Google Sheets, and posts a daily summary after all competitors are processed.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the schedule trigger for the desired daily run time and timezone.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and point the URL-reading and price-history update nodes to the correct spreadsheet, sheet, and columns.\n- Configure the HTTP Request node for any required headers, retry behavior, or authentication needed to access competitor pages.\n- Add OpenAI credentials and review the extraction prompt/model settings for price, stock, and confidence output.\n- Connect Slack credentials and set the destination channels for fetch failures, low-confidence alerts, price-drop alerts, and daily summaries.\n- Connect Notion credentials and select the database used to log significant price drops.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the competitor URL sheet schema, AI extraction prompt, low-confidence threshold, significant-drop percentage, Slack message formats, and Notion properties to match your monitoring rules."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
